{
  "about": [
    "How Find Lost Files knows a file by its start (signatures) and, for simple kinds, where it ends (ends).",
    "A signature: the type's id, the bytes it starts with as hex (?? for any byte), where they are (at, from the",
    "start of a sector; 0 if left out), and a check: a test in the code for what bytes alone can't say. Only the",
    "first signature of a group that fits counts. Order matters: the first type that measures right wins.",
    "An end, for types the code doesn't measure itself: a size kept in the file (size), a chain of pieces that",
    "each say how big they are (chunks), or bytes that close it (footer, then up to max bytes). Trailers that",
    "can follow: an APE tag (apetag) or an ID3 version 1 tag (id3v1)."
  ],
